# Project Cursor Rules - Flutter + AWS CDK Infrastructure

## Project Overview

This is a hybrid project containing:

- **Flutter mobile application** (iOS/Android) with Amplify integration
- **AWS CDK infrastructure** for backend services
- Focus: Event and Todo management features

## Core Principles

1. **Understandability First**: Code should be self-documenting and easy to comprehend
2. **Simplicity Over Cleverness**: Prefer straightforward solutions over complex optimizations
3. **Consistency**: Follow established patterns within the codebase
4. **Maintainability**: Write code that's easy to modify and extend

---

## Flutter Development Guidelines

### Code Organization

- Follow feature-first architecture in `lib/features/`
- Each feature should have clear separation: screens, widgets, services, models
- Keep `core/` for shared utilities, widgets, and services
- Place app-level configuration in `app/` directory

### Dart/Flutter Best Practices

#### 1. Widget Structure

```dart
// ✅ GOOD: Clear, named widgets with const constructors
class EventCard extends StatelessWidget {
  const EventCard({
    super.key,
    required this.event,
    this.onTap,
  });

  final Event event;
  final VoidCallback? onTap;

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    return Card(
      child: ListTile(
        title: Text(event.title),
        onTap: onTap,
      ),
    );
  }
}

// ❌ AVOID: Inline widgets, missing const
Widget buildEventCard(Event event) {
  return Card(child: ListTile(title: Text(event.title)));
}
```

#### 2. State Management

- Use simple state management (Provider, Riverpod, or built-in StatefulWidget)
- Avoid over-engineering state solutions
- Keep state close to where it's used
- Document state dependencies clearly

```dart
// ✅ GOOD: Clear state with descriptive names
class TodoScreenState extends State<TodoScreen> {
  bool _isLoading = false;
  List<Todo> _todos = [];
  String? _errorMessage;

  // Methods are clearly named and focused
  Future<void> _loadTodos() async {
    setState(() => _isLoading = true);
    try {
      _todos = await _todoService.fetchTodos();
    } catch (e) {
      _errorMessage = 'Failed to load todos: ${e.toString()}';
    } finally {
      setState(() => _isLoading = false);
    }
  }
}
```

#### 3. Naming Conventions

- Classes: `PascalCase` (EventCard, TodoService)
- Files: `snake_case` (event_card.dart, todo_service.dart)
- Variables/Functions: `camelCase` (eventTitle, loadTodos)
- Constants: `lowerCamelCase` for local, `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` for global
- Private members: prefix with `_` (\_isLoading, \_loadTodos)

#### 4. Error Handling

```dart
// ✅ GOOD: Explicit error handling with user feedback
Future<void> deleteEvent(String id) async {
  try {
    await _eventService.delete(id);
    _showSuccessMessage('Event deleted successfully');
  } on NetworkException catch (e) {
    _showErrorMessage('Network error: ${e.message}');
  } catch (e) {
    _showErrorMessage('Unexpected error occurred');
    debugPrint('Delete event error: $e');
  }
}

// ❌ AVOID: Silent failures
Future<void> deleteEvent(String id) async {
  try {
    await _eventService.delete(id);
  } catch (e) {
    // Silent failure - user doesn't know what happened
  }
}
```

#### 5. Async/Await

- Always use `async`/`await` instead of `.then()`
- Add `unawaited()` from `dart:async` for fire-and-forget operations
- Handle errors explicitly at appropriate levels

#### 6. Code Documentation

```dart
/// Displays a card for an event with title, date, and actions.
///
/// The card is tappable and can trigger navigation to event details.
/// Shows a countdown if the event is in the future.
class EventCard extends StatelessWidget {
  const EventCard({
    super.key,
    required this.event,
    this.onTap,
    this.showCountdown = true,
  });

  /// The event to display
  final Event event;

  /// Callback when card is tapped
  final VoidCallback? onTap;

  /// Whether to show countdown timer
  final bool showCountdown;

  // ... implementation
}
```

#### 7. Null Safety

- Use null-safety features properly (`?`, `!`, `??`, `?.`)
- Prefer `??` over `? :` for default values
- Avoid using `!` unless absolutely certain

```dart
// ✅ GOOD: Safe null handling
final title = event.title ?? 'Untitled Event';
final description = event.description?.trim() ?? '';

// ❌ AVOID: Risky null assertion
final title = event.title!; // Can crash if null
```

### UI/UX Guidelines

- Use `Theme.of(context)` for colors and text styles
- Prefer `const` constructors for better performance
- Extract repeated UI patterns into reusable widgets
- Keep build methods focused and readable (< 100 lines)
- Use meaningful spacing with `SizedBox` or padding constants

### Services & Business Logic

- Keep services in `features/[feature]/services/`
- One responsibility per service
- Use dependency injection where possible
- Mock services for testing

```dart
// ✅ GOOD: Focused service with clear interface
class TodoService {
  TodoService({required AmplifyDataStore dataStore})
      : _dataStore = dataStore;

  final AmplifyDataStore _dataStore;

  /// Fetches all todos for the current user
  Future<List<Todo>> fetchTodos() async {
    // Implementation
  }

  /// Creates a new todo
  Future<Todo> createTodo({
    required String title,
    String? description,
  }) async {
    // Implementation
  }
}
```

### Models

- Use immutable models with `@immutable` annotation
- Implement `copyWith`, `==`, and `hashCode` for data models
- Consider using code generation (freezed, json_serializable) for complex models

```dart
// ✅ GOOD: Clean, immutable model
@immutable
class Event {
  const Event({
    required this.id,
    required this.title,
    required this.date,
    this.description,
  });

  final String id;
  final String title;
  final DateTime date;
  final String? description;

  Event copyWith({
    String? title,
    DateTime? date,
    String? description,
  }) {
    return Event(
      id: id,
      title: title ?? this.title,
      date: date ?? this.date,
      description: description ?? this.description,
    );
  }
}
```

