## AWS CDK Guidelines

### Infrastructure as Code Principles

#### 1. Stack Organization

- One stack per logical environment/service
- Use nested stacks for complex architectures
- Keep stacks focused and manageable (< 200 LOC)

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: Focused, well-named stack
export class TodoApiStack extends cdk.Stack {
  constructor(scope: Construct, id: string, props?: cdk.StackProps) {
    super(scope, id, props);

    // API Gateway
    const api = new apigateway.RestApi(this, "TodoApi", {
      restApiName: "Todo Service",
      description: "API for todo management",
    });

    // Lambda function
    const todoHandler = new lambda.Function(this, "TodoHandler", {
      runtime: lambda.Runtime.NODEJS_18_X,
      handler: "index.handler",
      code: lambda.Code.fromAsset("lambda"),
    });

    // Connect resources
    const todosResource = api.root.addResource("todos");
    todosResource.addMethod(
      "GET",
      new apigateway.LambdaIntegration(todoHandler),
    );
  }
}
```

#### 2. Resource Naming

- Use descriptive, consistent names
- Include environment in resource names for multi-env deployments
- Follow AWS naming conventions

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: Clear, environment-aware naming
const todoTable = new dynamodb.Table(this, "TodoTable", {
  tableName: `${props.environment}-todos`,
  partitionKey: { name: "userId", type: dynamodb.AttributeType.STRING },
  sortKey: { name: "todoId", type: dynamodb.AttributeType.STRING },
});

// ❌ AVOID: Vague names
const table = new dynamodb.Table(this, "Table1", {
  tableName: "data",
});
```

#### 3. Configuration Management

- Use CDK context for environment-specific values
- Keep secrets in AWS Secrets Manager or Parameter Store
- Document all configuration options

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: Externalized configuration
interface TodoStackProps extends cdk.StackProps {
  environment: "dev" | "staging" | "prod";
  tableCapacity?: {
    readCapacity: number;
    writeCapacity: number;
  };
}

export class TodoStack extends cdk.Stack {
  constructor(scope: Construct, id: string, props: TodoStackProps) {
    super(scope, id, props);

    const capacity = props.tableCapacity ?? {
      readCapacity: 5,
      writeCapacity: 5,
    };

    // Use configuration
  }
}
```

#### 4. Security Best Practices

- Apply principle of least privilege for IAM roles
- Enable encryption at rest and in transit
- Use VPC for sensitive resources
- Never hardcode credentials

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: Minimal IAM permissions
todoHandler.addToRolePolicy(
  new iam.PolicyStatement({
    effect: iam.Effect.ALLOW,
    actions: ["dynamodb:GetItem", "dynamodb:Query", "dynamodb:PutItem"],
    resources: [todoTable.tableArn],
  }),
);

// ❌ AVOID: Overly permissive
todoHandler.addToRolePolicy(
  new iam.PolicyStatement({
    effect: iam.Effect.ALLOW,
    actions: ["dynamodb:*"],
    resources: ["*"],
  }),
);
```

#### 5. Tagging Strategy

- Tag all resources for cost tracking and organization
- Include: Environment, Project, Owner, CostCenter

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: Comprehensive tagging
cdk.Tags.of(this).add("Environment", props.environment);
cdk.Tags.of(this).add("Project", "EventCountdown");
cdk.Tags.of(this).add("ManagedBy", "CDK");
```

#### 6. Construct Reusability

- Extract common patterns into custom constructs
- Share constructs across stacks when appropriate

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: Reusable construct
export class ApiLambdaConstruct extends Construct {
  public readonly handler: lambda.Function;
  public readonly api: apigateway.RestApi;

  constructor(scope: Construct, id: string, props: ApiLambdaProps) {
    super(scope, id);

    this.handler = new lambda.Function(this, "Handler", {
      runtime: lambda.Runtime.NODEJS_18_X,
      handler: props.handler,
      code: lambda.Code.fromAsset(props.codePath),
      environment: props.environment,
    });

    this.api = new apigateway.RestApi(this, "Api", {
      restApiName: props.apiName,
    });
  }
}
```

